00:04:00.407 --> 00:04:01.860
(audience claps)

00:04:01.860 --> 00:04:04.920
So Ani deals with many societal pressures.

00:04:04.920 --> 00:04:06.600
As a young woman yourself,

00:04:06.600 --> 00:04:08.010
how do you deal with societal pressures?

00:04:08.010 --> 00:04:09.690
'Cause like again, I, you grew up in a

00:04:09.690 --> 00:04:11.100
different environment than we did.

00:04:11.100 --> 00:04:13.920
- Yeah. I mean, I think there's
a lot of pressure today.

00:04:13.920 --> 00:04:15.780
I think friends place pressure on you,

00:04:15.780 --> 00:04:17.160
Family can place pressure on you.

00:04:17.160 --> 00:04:19.320
Society, in general,
places a lot of pressure.

00:04:19.320 --> 00:04:22.380
There's a lot of expectation
about who you're supposed to be

00:04:22.380 --> 00:04:23.490
and how you're supposed to act,

00:04:23.490 --> 00:04:24.780
and how you're supposed to seem.

00:04:24.780 --> 00:04:26.160
And something we've talked about a lot

00:04:26.160 --> 00:04:28.410
is the difference between,
you know, the person

00:04:28.410 --> 00:04:30.810
or persona that you present,
you know, on the internet,

00:04:30.810 --> 00:04:33.510
especially as an actress, where,
you know, you want to feel

00:04:33.510 --> 00:04:36.810
like you're perfect all the
time, which is not human.

00:04:36.810 --> 00:04:38.220
Humans are not perfect.

00:04:38.220 --> 00:04:39.750
We're not meant to be perfect.

00:04:39.750 --> 00:04:41.211
We're meant to make mistakes and mess up

00:04:41.211 --> 00:04:44.850
and, and, and do things
wrong, and learn and grow.

00:04:44.850 --> 00:04:46.200
Like, how are you supposed to get older

00:04:46.200 --> 00:04:49.260
if you can never, you
know learn from mistakes.

00:04:49.260 --> 00:04:51.780
You're just gonna be
stunted pretty much forever.

00:04:51.780 --> 00:04:52.740
- [Kelly] Yeah.
- So I think

00:04:52.740 --> 00:04:55.110
there's a huge pressure
when it comes to that.

00:04:55.110 --> 00:04:57.030
I mean, I, we were talking
about how we, you know,

00:04:57.030 --> 00:04:59.910
I grew up with social
media and Mila didn't,

00:04:59.910 --> 00:05:02.220
and that is hard, it's really hard.

00:05:02.220 --> 00:05:03.053
- [Kelly] Yeah.
- [Mila] But you're also

00:05:03.053 --> 00:05:05.580
incredible at not feeding into it.

00:05:05.580 --> 00:05:06.840
We've talked about this.
- Well, thank you.

00:05:06.840 --> 00:05:08.160
- You're very good at separating

00:05:08.160 --> 00:05:09.840
what you do and who you are.

00:05:09.840 --> 00:05:12.120
- That's very difficult for adults,

00:05:12.120 --> 00:05:14.393
let alone young individuals.

00:05:14.393 --> 00:05:16.620
- I know, I think that you're
gonna, you're gonna be fine.

00:05:16.620 --> 00:05:18.960
But like, but I think that that's the

00:05:18.960 --> 00:05:21.646
the minority in this twenty
something year old industry.

00:05:21.646 --> 00:05:22.479
- [Kelly] Yeah.

